<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  Deliberately empty (ADR-0008).

  Entitlements under the hardened runtime are relaxations: each one hands back
  a protection the runtime would otherwise enforce. toolog asks for none, so it
  keeps all of them. Library validation stays on, JIT and unsigned executable
  memory stay off, dyld environment overrides are ignored, and the process
  cannot be attached to by a debugger it did not consent to.

  This file exists rather than being left out so the claim is a line in the
  repository instead of an absence nobody would notice being filled in. It is
  asserted by `the_shipped_app_asks_for_no_entitlements` in tests/bundle.rs,
  and anyone holding a built copy can confirm it for themselves by asking
  codesign to display the entitlements of the installed application.

  Editing note: XML forbids two consecutive hyphens inside a comment, and
  codesign's entitlement parser rejects the entire file when it finds them
  while plutil reports the same file as valid. So no command line spelling a
  long option can be written here, which is why the check above is described
  rather than quoted.
-->
<dict>
</dict>
</plist>
